From 65aa381f70feec96a15c0e129d759d8463fcff75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:41:52 +0300
Subject: debrand: drop upstream feedback, donate and changelog entries

This instance is not stoat.chat. Feedback pointed at upstream's GitHub
discussions, where reports about a modified self-hosted build are noise;
Donate pointed at upstream's ko-fi, and soliciting donations to a third
party from inside a private instance is not this build's business; What's
New fetched a changelog describing releases this instance does not track.

The "Stoat" settings category becomes "Integrations", the desktop version
label drops the product name, and the page title and PWA manifest are
neutral.

Source Code is deliberately kept. Stoat is AGPL-3.0 and this is a modified
version offered to users over a network, which is what section 13 covers:
those users must be offered the corresponding source of THIS build. The
href still points upstream and must be repointed at wherever this fork is
published before accounts are handed out.
